    dct:description "A UCC financing statement can be used for all types of collateral, while an EFS (Effective Financing Statement) specifically applies to farm products. This means an EFS must be more specific about the description of the farm products, including the crop year, quantity, and the specific county where they are produced to properly notify potential buyers of a security interest in those goods. The Master List compiles all EFS filings and includes new filings, all active filings, and updates to existing filings."@en ;
